    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode de-duplication in `OwnerRestControllerV1.customerCode(...)` at `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:475`.\n\nThe method previously returned the raw `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'` code. Now, after computing that base code, it:\n1. Collects all existing owners' non-null `customerCode` values into a `Set`.\n2. Returns the base code unchanged if it's unique.\n3. Otherwise appends `'-<n>'`, starting at `n = 2` and incrementing to the smallest value that yields a code not already in use, then returns that de-duplicated code.\n\nI also added the required imports (`java.util.Set`, `java.util.stream.Collectors`).\n\n**Test result:** `BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (`AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique`, the one test class in the project, passes).\n\nNote: the acceptance test verifies the rule's guarantee (distinct owners always get distinct customerCodes) rather than forcing a genuine hash collision \u2014 which, as its comment explains, can't be triggered black-box because telephone-uniqueness already prevents identical `telephone + lastName` inputs. The dedup logic itself handles the collision case directly per the spec.",
